  "result": "I found the bug but haven't changed any code, because plan mode is on. I couldn't call ExitPlanMode here, so I'm giving you the plan in this message.\n\n**Cause:** `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py:754` returns `bound - dir` for open bounds. The direction is `1` when clamping up to `min` and `-1` when clamping down to `max`, so the subtraction moves the value away from the range:\n- `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` turns `-5` into `-1`, when it should be `1`.\n- `IntRange(max=5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` turns `9` into `6`, when it should be `4`.\n\n**Fix:** change that line to `return bound + dir`.\n\n**Tests:** I'd add two cases next to the existing clamp ones in `tests/test_types.py` (around line 23): `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` on `\"-5\"` giving `1`, and `IntRange(max=5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` on `\"9\"` giving `4`. Then I'd run `pytest tests/test_types.py tests/test_info_dict.py`.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\some-users-report-that-lexical-harbor.md`. Say the word and I'll apply it.",
